{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested for exact head 9c7a96b09b53384d968953341abc691fca4e1c58. Architecture: this head correctly limits the contract change to layer 7, keeps Table as the default board presentation, reuses the existing thread and projected-work population contracts, updates docs/reference/architecture.md in the same head, and does not change layers 2, 3, 5, or 6. Three implementation defects prevent the documented layer-7 contract from being true. First, buildOutcomeMap selects a focal card state from the last WorkRow for a thread but selects waitsOn independently from the last projection commitment. With several commitments for one request, serialization order changes the card and can render a satisfied card that says Waits on worker from a different live commitment. Define one deterministic thread-level aggregation that keeps state and waiting_on from the same projected row, and add reversed-order and mixed-lifecycle regressions. Second, Fit to view clamps scale at 0.35; a legal 160-card one-column or many-layer graph needs a much smaller scale, so the control does not fit the graph it promises to fit. Use a safe scale derived from actual layout and viewport dimensions and test a nonzero viewport with the largest legal layouts. Third, contributorsPerEdge is checked only after every contributor has been retained and deduplicated with a linear scan. One admitted record may carry 4096 causal references; an independent 4096-contributor fixture took about 564 ms merely to omit its edge. Enforce the complete-edge bound during accumulation, retaining at most the limit plus overflow evidence, and keep relation-group selection bounded without exposing a partial line. Add a mutation-sensitive high-cardinality regression. Security and authority: React escaping, direct-only evidence, exact identifiers, malformed-event handling, cycle handling, pointer capture, and output cardinality are otherwise sound; no signing endpoint or fold authority changes. But the governing request 4501760d has no structural bases, old authorization assert aa61afe1 is stale and unratified, and notes/2026-08-30-outcome-map.md still states candidate design with no UI implementation authorized. Before approval, publish a fresh exact-head artifact for the governing design, file an ordinary adoption proposal resting on that artifact, obtain Hugh ratification, and make the fresh review request rest on the ratified proposal as well as every implementation artifact. This records the user-authorized reinstatement durably instead of relying on stale prose. Simplification: the local pure projection and layout modules are preferable to adding a graph dependency, and the Table/Graph switch shares one population without duplicating list logic. Keep that shape; centralize the card selection policy and scale clamp rather than adding special cases. Independent gates passed: clean exact child of d09a5a8d0, git diff --check, npm test 176/176, npm build, make ui-check with byte-clean embed, make docs, make vet, make test, make build, and clean tree.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:23a36974c93d4ac95c73ae95f0c9accc209246f2","head":"9c7a96b09b53384d968953341abc691fca4e1c58","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:6cc845dead2299ba7b5b3fad9e5aabc22b8c9722\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:afc6303fb0929f49a6fe729ad666761fff801569","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}